\nL95: \nL96: 3,445人\nL97: \nL98: 電子報訂閱人數\nL99: \nL100: 223,145人\nL101:   * 本網站係提供法規之最新動態資訊及資料檢索，並不提供法規及法律諮詢之服務。\nL102:   * 若有任何法律上的疑義，建議您可逕向發布法規之主管機關洽詢。\nL103:   * 本網站法規資料係由政府各機關提供之電子檔或書面文字登打製作，若與各法規主管機關之公布文字有所不同，仍以各法規主管機關之公布資料為準。\nL104:   * 部分資料內容，使用特殊文字或符號，如欲詳閱內容，請連結至【33†司法院網站†www.judicial.gov.tw】下載造字檔。\nL105:   * 全國法規資料庫之內容每週五定期更新，當週發布之法律、命令資料，將於完成法規整編作業後，於下週五更新上線。\nL106:   * 法規整編資料截止日：民國 115 年 10 月 16 日\nL107:   * 瀏覽人次總計：1,650,694,071人\nL108:   * 本月瀏覽人次：16,981,620人\nL109:   * 目前使用人次：3,445人\nL110:   * 電子報訂閱：223,145人\nL111: \nL112: │ 【34†政府網站資料開放宣告】 │ 【35†隱私權保護宣告】 │ 【36†資訊安全政策†www.moj.gov.tw】 │ 【37†Q & A】 │ 【38†意見回饋】 │ 【39†API文件】 │\nL113: 本網站由法務部全國法規資料庫工作小組維運管理...\nL114: \nL115: 法務部地址：100204 台北市重慶南路一段130號　電話：(02)2191-0189\nL116: 第二辦公室地址：100006 台北市貴陽街1段235號　電話：(02)2191-0189\nL117: \nL118: 【40†Image: 榮獲第14屆全國標準化獎-團體標準化獎】\nL119: \nL120: 【8†回上方】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n金融監督管理委員會主管法規共用系統-法規內容-動產擔保交易法施行細則 (https://law.fsc.gov.tw/LawContent.aspx?id=GL000440)\nciteturn1714view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://law.fsc.gov.tw/LawContent.aspx?id=GL000440\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 163\nL0: 您的瀏覽器不支援JavaScript功能，若網頁功能無法正常使用時，請開啟瀏覽器JavaScript狀態\nL1: \nL2: [Input]\nL3: \nL4: [Input] [Input]\nL5: \nL6: 【0†跳到主要內容區塊】\nL7: \nL8: 主管法規查詢系統\nL9: \nL10: 主管法規查詢系統\nL11: \nL12:   * 【1†最新訊息】\nL13:   * 【2†法規體系】\nL14:   * 【3†法規檢索】\nL15:   *   *   * 【4†草案預告】\nL16:   * 【5†相關網站】\nL17:   * 【6†網站導覽】\nL18:   * 【7†使用手冊】\nL19:   * 【1†回首頁】\nL20:   * 【8†English】\nL21: \nL22: 【9†:::】\nL23: \nL24: 【10† 友善列印】\nL25: ## 法規內容\nL26: \nL27: 法規名稱：  | 動產擔保交易法施行細則【11†英】\nL28: 公發布日：  | 民國 54 年 06 月 07 日\nL29: 修正日期：  | 民國 104 年 12 月 17 日\nL30: 發文字號：  | 院臺金字第1040039090號 令\nL31: 法規體系：  | 銀行局/動產擔保交易\nL32: 立法理由：  |\nL33: \nL34:   * 【12†動產擔保交易法施行細則 總說明（104.12.17）.pdf】\nL35:   * 【13†動產擔保交易法施行細則 條文對照表（104.12.17）.pdf】\nL36: 法規功能按鈕區\nL37: \nL38:   * 【14†法規內容】\nL39:   *   * 【15†條文檢索】\nL40:   *   * 【16†法規沿革】\nL41:   * 【17†歷史法規】\nL42:   *   *   * 第 1 條 本細則依動產擔保交易法（以下簡稱本法）第四十二條規定訂定之。\nL43: 第 2 條\nL44: 本法第六條所定動產擔保交易之登記機關如下：\nL45: 一、加工出口區內之標的物，以經濟部加工出口區管理處為登記機關。\nL46: 二、科學工業園區內之標的物，以科技部所屬各科學工業園區管理局為登\nL47:     記機關。\nL48: 三、農業科技園區內之標的物，以農業科技園區管理機關為登記機關。\nL49: 四、總噸位未滿二十之動力船舶或未滿五十之非動力船舶，以交通部航港\nL50:     局為登記機關。\nL51: 五、汽車、機車及拖車，以交通部公路總局為登記機關。\nL52: 六、前五款以外之標的物，其所在地或設籍在直轄市者，以直轄市政府為\nL53:     登記機關；在直轄市以外區域者，以經濟部為登記機關。\nL54: 前項第一款之登記機關，其設有分處者，得委任其分處代辦登記。\nL55: 第一項第五款之登記機關，得委任辦理公路監理業務之監理機關代辦登記\nL56: 。\nL57: \nL58: 第 3 條\nL59: 動產擔保交易登記，應由契約當事人或其代理人向登記機關申請之。\nL60: 登記事項之內容有變更時，應由契約當事人或其代理人檢具證明文件向原\nL61: 登記機關申請變更登記。\nL62: 前二項申請，得以網路傳輸方式向統一線上登記及公示網站為之；申請註\nL63: 銷登記、抄錄及核發證明書，亦同。\nL64: 以前項方式申請者，視同向登記機關申請。\nL65: 第 4 條\nL66: 依本法第七條第一項規定申請登記時，應檢具下列各項文件：\nL67: 一、登記申請書。\nL68: 二、由代理人申請登記者，其本人之委託書。\nL69: 三、登記原因之契約或其複本。\nL70: 四、契約當事人之證明文件。\nL71: 五、標的物有所有權證明文件或使用執照者，其文件或執照。\nL72: 六、標的物設定抵押權須經主管機關核准者，其核准文件。\nL73: 七、債務人無第七條規定各款情事之切結。\nL74: 前項各款申請文件，得依電子簽章法之規定，以電子文件為之。\nL75: \nL76: 第 5 條\nL77: 動產擔保交易之登記事項如下：\nL78: 一、動產抵押權之登記。\nL79: 二、附條件買賣之登記。\nL80: 三、信託占有之登記。\nL81: 四、延長有效期間之登記。\nL82: 五、標的物所有權人變更之登記。\nL83: 六、標的物變更之登記。\nL84: 七、動產擔保權註銷之登記。\nL85: 八、其他有關之登記。\nL86: 前項登記，由登記機關就第四條申請文件於形式上查對其所載事項與申請\nL87: 登記事項是否相符後為之。\nL88: 第 6 條\nL89: 第四條第一項第一款之登記申請書應記載下列事項：\nL90: 一、登記原因。\nL91: 二、登記標的物之名稱及其型式、規格、廠牌、數量、製造廠商、引擎號\nL92:     碼、出廠年月日、所在地、領有執照者其執照號碼。\nL93: 三、登記機關。\nL94: 四、申請之年月日。\nL95: 五、申請人之姓名或名稱、出生年月日、國民身分證統一編號、公司或商\nL96:     業統一編號或扣繳單位統一編號、住居所或營業所。\nL97: 六、由代理人申請時，並記其代理人之姓名、國民身分證統一編號、出生\nL98:     年月日、住所。\nL99: 七、擔保債權種類及其金額。\nL100: 八、其他應記明之事項。\nL101: 前項第二款事項，經當事人以契約約定者，得以登記標的物之名稱、數量\nL102: 、所在地等足以特定該標的物之一般性說明為之。\nL103: \nL104: 第 7 條\nL105: 有下列各款情形之一者，不得申請為動產擔保交易之登記：\nL106: 一、債務人曾受破產宣告尚未復權，或破產程序在進行中。\nL107: 二、債務人就標的物未具有完整之所有權。\nL108: 三、標的物係屬假扣押或假處分之標的。\nL109: \nL110: 第 8 條\nL111: 登記機關應備下列登記書表簿冊：\nL112: 一、登記申請書。\nL113: 二、登記收件簿。\nL114: 三、登記簿。\nL115: 四、登記索引簿。\nL116: 五、其他書表簿冊。\nL117: 前項各種書表簿冊，由登記機關規定格式印製，並得以電腦處理之。\nL118: 第 9 條\nL119: 登記機關所備登記簿，應記載登記契約當事人之姓名或名稱、國民身分證\nL120: 統一編號、公司或商業統一編號或扣繳單位統一編號、住居所或營業所、\nL121: 訂立契約日期、標的物說明、價格、擔保債權種類及其金額、有效期間等\nL122: ；遇有變更登記者，其變更事項及年月日。\nL123: 前項變更登記以附記為之，附記作成後，應將原登記應變更部分塗銷之。\nL124: \nL125: 第 10 條\nL126: 登記機關接受登記之申請後，應於三個工作日內將登記事項辦理完竣，並\nL127: 發給登記證明書正副本各一份。\nL128: \nL129: 第 11 條\nL130: 登記機關於辦竣登記後，應依本法第八條規定公開於統一線上登記及公示\nL131: 網站或以其他適當方法公告之。\nL132: 前項統一線上登記及公示網站為集中資料庫，並得以債務人之姓名或名稱\nL133: 檢索。\nL134: \nL135: 第 12 條\nL136: 登記機關於年度終了後，應將上年度登記繼續有效部分之各項紀錄，轉列\nL137: 於當年度登記內，以便查考。\nL138: 第 13 條\nL139: 登記機關辦理動產擔保交易登記時，依下列基準收取規費：\nL140: 一、登記費（包括證書費）新臺幣九百元。\nL141: 二、變更登記費（包括證書費）新臺幣四百五十元。\nL142: 三、註銷登記費免收。\nL143: 四、查閱費（包括謄本費或影印費）新臺幣一百二十元。\nL144: 五、補發證書費新臺幣一百二十元。\nL145: 六、電腦資料抄錄費，每次抄錄筆數在五百筆以內者，新臺幣三千元。每\nL146:     次抄錄筆數超過五百筆時，每增加一筆另繳納抄錄費新臺幣二元。\nL147: 前項第一款至第五款規費，如擔保債權金額在新臺幣九萬元以下者，減半\nL148: 收取。\nL149: \nL150: 第 14 條\nL151: 本細則除第二條自中華民國一百零五年一月一日施行外，自發布日施行。\nL152: \nL153: 【18†:::】\nL154: \nL155: 【19†政府網站資料開放宣告 │†www.fsc.gov.tw】 【20†隱私權保護宣告 │†www.fsc.gov.tw】 【21†資訊安全政策 │†www.fsc.gov.tw】\nL156:   * 金融監督管理委員會 版權所有 220232 新北市板橋區縣民大道二段7號18樓 　電話：(02)8968-0899　傳真：(02)8969-1215\nL157:   * 本會駐紐約代表辦事處:1 E.42 Street, 13F, New York, NY 10017, U.S.A. 聯絡電話:(1-212) 317-7326\nL158:   * 本會駐倫敦代表辦事處:46-48 Grosvenor Gardens London SW1W 0EB, UK 聯絡電話:(44-20)7628-1501\nL159:   * 系統版本：115.09.10\nL160:   * 系統更新日期：115.09.29\nL161: \nL162: 【22†回上方】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn1714view2 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ppstrq.nat.gov.tw/pps/web/Show/B1Page.do\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://ppstrq.nat.gov.tw/pps/web/Show/B1Page.do: (503) Service Unavailable\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBureau of Consular Affairs, Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Republic of China(Taiwan)-Visa-Exempt Entry (https://www.boca.gov.tw/cp-149-4486-7785a-2.html)\nciteturn1714view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.boca.gov.tw/cp-149-4486-7785a-2.html\",\"lineno\":46}); Total lines: 149\nL0: 【0†GTM†www.googletagmanager.com】 【1†Go to main content area】\nL1: \nL2: 【2†:::】\nL3: \nL4: #\nL5: \nL6: [Button: search]\nL7: \nL8: Full site search\nL9: \nL10: [Input: Keyword]  [Input]\nL11: \nL12: [Input]\nL13: \nL14: Popular keywords：\nL15: \nL16:   * Visa\nL17:   * Passport\nL18: \nL19: Your browser does not seem to support JavaScript syntax, but it does not matter, it does not affect the presentation of the content.\nL20: \nL21: 【3†:::】\nL22: ## Visa-Exempt Entry\nL23: \nL24:   * facebook\nL25:   * twitter\nL26:   * line\nL27:   * 【4†Print】\nL28:   * Go Back( alt + ← Go Back)\nL29: \nL30:   * Created：2026-07-17\nL31:   * Data Source：Bureau Of Consular Affairs\nL32:   * Counter：1708966\nL33:   * Updated：2026-07-17\nL34: \nL35: Visa-Exempt Entry\nL36: Type  | Visa-Exempt Entry\nL37: --- | ---\nL38: Foreign nationals eligible for visa-exempt entry  |\nL39:   1.\nL40: Nationals of the following countries are eligible for the visa-exemption program, with a duration of stay of up to 90 days: Albania, Andorra, Australia, Austria, Belgium, Bulgaria, Canada, Chile, Croatia, Cyprus, Czech Republic, Denmark, Estonia, Eswatini*, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Guatemala, Holy See, Hungary, Iceland, Ireland, Israel, Italy, Japan*, Kosovo, Republic of Korea, Latvia, Liechtenstein, Lithuania, Luxembourg, Malta, Marshall Islands*, Monaco, Netherlands, New Zealand, North Macedonia*(effective until March 31, 2030), Norway, Palau, Paraguay, Poland, Portugal, Romania, San Marino, Slovakia, Slovenia, Spain, Sweden, Switzerland, Tuvalu*, United Kingdom*, and United States of America*.\nL41:   2. Nationals of the following countries are eligible for the visa-exemption program, with a duration of stay of up to 30 days: Belize*, Malaysia, Saint Kitts and Nevis*, Saint Lucia*, Saint Vincent and the Grenadines, and Singapore.\nL42:   3. Nationals of Honduras*, except those holding diplomatic or official/service passports, are eligible for the visa-exemption program, with a duration of stay of up to 90 days.\nL43:   4. Nationals of Dominican Republic, except those holding diplomatic or official/service passports, are eligible for the visa-exemption program, with a duration of stay of up to 30 days.\nL44:   5. Nationals of Oman are eligible for the visa-exemption program, with a duration of stay of up to 14 days.\nL45:   6. Nationals of the Kingdom of Thailand (effective until July 31, 2027), except those holding diplomatic or official/service passports, are eligible for the visa-exemption program, with a duration of stay of up to 14 days.\nL46:   7. Nationals of Brunei (effective until July 31, 2027), except those holding diplomatic or official/ service passports, are eligible for the visa-exemption program, with a duration of stay of up to 14 days. In addition, those holding a Brunei Certificate of Identity are eligible for the visa-exemption program, with a duration of stay of up to 14 days.\nL47:   8. Nationals of the Philippines (effective until July 31, 2027), except those holding diplomatic or official/service passports, are eligible for the visa-exemption program, with a duration of stay of up to 14 days.\nL48: Requirements  |\nL49:   1. A passport with remaining validity of at least six months as of the date of entry\nL50:      * Visa-exempt entry only applies to foreign visitors holding formal passports (i.e., ordinary, official/service and diplomatic passports). Those holding emergency, temporary, or other informal passports or travel documents are ineligible, with the exception of those holding a Brunei Certificate of Identity.\nL51:      * Holders of Belize, Eswatini, Saint Kitts and Nevis, Saint Lucia, and Tuvalu passports with place of birth recorded on the passport data page as Afghanistan, Iran, Iraq, Libya, Nigeria, Pakistan, the People's Republic of China, Syria, and Yemen are ineligible for the visa exemption. Holders of Honduran passports with place of birth recorded on the passport data page as the People's Republic of China are also ineligible for the visa exemption.\nL52:      * A national of the Republic of the Marshall Islands shall mean any person who holds the nationality of the Republic of the Marshall Islands and is confined to the following categories：(1) a person who acquired the citizenship of the Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands at birth before the effective date of the Constitution of the Republic of the Marshall Islands, and has become and remains a citizen of the Republic of the Marshall Islands; or (2) a person who acquired the citizenship of the Republic of the Marshall Islands at birth, on or after the effective date of the Constitution of the Republic of the Marshall Islands.\nL53:      * USA nationals who possess a passport, including an emergency passports, valid for the intended period of stay are eligible for visa-exempt entry.\nL54:      * Japan nationals who possess a passport valid for the intended period of stay are eligible for visa-exempt entry.\nL55:      * Holders of emergency or temporary passport, except those from the United States of America, should apply for a visa at a Taiwan (ROC) overseas mission, or a landing visa after arriving in the Taiwan (ROC).\nL56:   2. Only the United Kingdom passport holders with British Citizen status are eligible for visa-exempt entry.\nL57:   3. A confirmed return air/sea ticket or air/sea ticket and a visa for the next destination, and a confirmed seat reservation for departure flight.\nL58:   4. Not determined by immigration officers at ports of entry in Taiwan (ROC) to be otherwise ineligible.\nL59:   5. Holders of Brunei, Philippines and Thailand passports must have proof of accommodation (hotel) booking, host/sponsor's contact information and sufficient travel funds.\nL60:   6. Brunei, Philippines and Thailand vessel/aircraft crew members or service personnel intending to board to report for duty are ineligible for the visa-exempt entry.\nL61: Duration of stay  |\nL62:   1. The duration of stay starts from the day after arrival and is not extendable. Foreign visitors must depart by the end of the said duration. 【5†Please click here for information on penalties for overstay.†www.immigration.gov.tw】\nL63:   2. Visa-exempt entry cannot be converted to visa-based stay, unless any of the following applies:\nL64:     1. In the event of situations that prevent them from leaving Taiwan (ROC), such as severe acute illness, natural disaster, or other force majeure.\nL65:     2. White-collar professionals who have obtained (i) a work permit granted for a period under 6 months within their permitted duration of stay, or (ii) a work permit for fulfilling contract purpose issued before or within 30 days of their entry (Brunei, North Macedonia, Philippines and Thailand are not included) may apply for a work visa.\nL66: *All applications shall be submitted within 8 working days before their permitted duration of stay expires.\nL67: *In accordance with National Immigration Agency (NIA) regulations, those foreigners who come to Taiwan (ROC) to engage in contracting work for more than 6 months, enter Taiwan (ROC) under a visa-exemption program, and plan to apply for an alien residence certificate from the Immigration Agency, Ministry of the Interior, are required to simultaneously submit applications for visitor and resident visas to this Bureau or the Central, Southern, Eastern, and Yunjianan Offices of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.\nL68: *Those foreigners who obtain work permits (exclude fulfilling contract purpose) granted for a period over 6 months shall apply for residency directly to the National Immigration Agency in accordance with the Act for the Recruitment and Employment of Foreign Professionals.\nL69:     3. Canadian and UK passport holders are eligible for the visa-exemption program with a duration of stay of 90 days which is extendable up to 180 days, please refer to the 【6†Notice for British & Canadian Passport Holders Who Enter Taiwan (ROC) Visa-Free and Apply for an Extension of Stay】.\nL70:   3. The visa-exemption trial program for nationals of Russia expired (effective until July 31, 2022). (Extension of the trial program is under evaluation.)\nL71:   4. If Omani passport holders plan to stay in Taiwan (ROC) for more than 14 days, they may apply for an eVisa. For further requirements and additional information, please visit our website at https://visawebapp.boca.gov.tw/BOCA_EVISA/MRV04FORM.do.\nL72: Ports of entry  | Taiwan Taoyuan International Airport, Taipei Songshan Airport, Taichung International Airport, Chiayi Airport, Tainan Airport, Kaohsiung International Airport, Taitung Airport, Hualien Airport, Kinmen Airport, Magong Airport, Keelung Harbor, Taipei Harbor, Taichung Harbor, Kaohsiung Harbor, Hualien Harbor, Shuitou Harbor, and Fu'ao Harbor.\nL73: Remarks:\nL74:   1. Those who have entered Taiwan (ROC) visa-free for purposes that do not require a permit—such as engaging in tourism, visiting friends or relatives, attending social events, conducting business, attending exhibitions, and engaging in fact-finding missions or international exchanges—who then intend to engage in activities that, according to the laws and regulations of relevant agencies, do require a permit must still obtain such a permit.\nL75: Those who intend to enter Taiwan (ROC) for purposes that require qualifications, such as religious work, must obtain a visa from a Taiwan (ROC) overseas mission before entering Taiwan (ROC).\nL76:   2.  According to Article 14 of the Regulations for Exit of Draftees, a draftee who has maintained his household registration in Taiwan (ROC) must enter into and depart from Taiwan (ROC) with his Taiwan (ROC) passport; a person who is subject to conscription and enters into Taiwan (ROC) with a foreign passport will be restricted from departing Taiwan (ROC).\nL77:   3.  Within seven days prior to arriving in Taiwan (ROC), please complete an online immigration arrival card (【7†https://twac.immigration.gov.tw†twac.immigration.gov.tw】) on the website of the National Immigration Agency.\nL78: \nL79: For conscription law, please visit the following website: 【8†http://www.immigration.gov.tw†www.immigration.gov.tw】\nL80: \nL81: [Button: Close]\nL82:   * 【9†Passport】\nL83:     * 【10†Apply for a Passport(Taiwan)】\nL84:     * 【11†Apply for a Passport(Abroad)】\nL85:     * 【12†Passport Photos】\nL86:     * 【13†Application Directions for a Second ROC Passport】\nL87:     * 【14†Applying for Past Passport Records】\nL88:     * 【15†Passport FAQs】\nL89:     * 【16†Application Forms】\nL90:     * 【17†Passport Act and Regulations】\nL91:     * 【18†ePassport Project】\nL92:     * 【19†Operating Directions for Issuance of Entry Permits】\nL93:     * 【20†Country Signing CA (CSCA) Information】\nL94:   * 【21†Visa】\nL95:     * 【22†General Information】\nL96:     * 【23†On-line Application Forms (not applicable to Hong Kong, Macau and PRC passport holders)†visawebapp.boca.gov.tw】\nL97:     * 【6†Visa-Exempt Entry, Landing Visa and eVisa】\nL98:     * 【24†Visitor Visas】\nL99:     * 【25†Resident Visas】\nL100:     * 【26†Study in Taiwan】\nL101:     * 【27†Southeast Asian Countries】\nL102:     * 【28†Working Holidays Scheme】\nL103:     * 【29†Entrepreneur】\nL104:     * 【30†Employment-Seeking】\nL105:     * 【31†Visa FAQs】\nL106:   * 【32†Authentication】\nL107:     * 【33†Document Authentication in ROC(Taiwan)】\nL108:     * 【34†Document Authentication Services】\nL109:     * 【35†Authentication of domestic documents】\nL110:     * 【36†Authentication of foreign documents】\nL111:     * 【37†Authentication Regulations】\nL112:     * 【38†Consular District】\nL113:     * 【39†Application Forms】\nL114:     * 【40†Authentication FAQs】\nL115:     * 【41†E-register】\nL116:   * 【42†Online Service】\nL117:     * 【23†On-line Application Forms(not applicable to Hong Kong,Macau and PRC passport holders)†visawebapp.boca.gov.tw】\nL118:     * 【43†Authentication-Application Progress†docauth.boca.gov.tw】\nL119:     * 【44†Authentication-Verification of Authentication†docauth.boca.gov.tw】\nL120:   * 【45†News & Events】\nL121:   * 【46†Our Locations】\nL122:   * 【47†Embassies and Missions】\n"
